{"kind":"artifact","text":"Exact-head implementation artifact for #10475 at internal/workroom, head eb64fbce6817576c55e0b0446fb41e8ab835cd44 on branch request/stale-because-row-v2 (pushed; first parent 1a299e207ff90d433f09078970fc38906a9f8990 is the repair commit, tree byte-identical to it).\n\nTHE FIX, answering dissent #11070 against head c9280b32. The old nearestRetiredBasis walk (fold.go ~2383-2422) breadth-first'd rests_on edges and named whatever retired node was nearest by hops then citation order, ignoring succeeded pointer-moves, exempt kinds and merge-plan skips — so it could name a retirement that caused nothing, and reported \"truncated\" past four hops. The cause is now named on the exact edge that fires staleness inside stalenessOf itself (stalenessFacts.because/becausePath): a directly retired basis names its own retiring supersession via a once-per-scope retirer index; propagated staleness inherits the intermediate's cause, which by construction is the originating retirement upstream; two independent causes resolve to the earliest-landed retirer. No hop budget, citation order decides nothing. Callers rewired; stale_because_truncated removed everywhere.\n\nPINS: TestStaleRowsNameTheActThatRetiredTheirBasis (direct), TestPropagatedStalenessNamesTheOriginatingRetirement (the discriminator the old walk fails), TestPropagatedCauseReachesPastAnyHopBudget, TestTwoIndependentCausesNameTheEarlierRetirement. Golden legacy_projection.golden.json moved stale_because from victim to retiring act.\n\nTESTS AND CONDITIONS MET at this exact head: go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test ./internal/workroom/... ./internal/statusview/... -count=1 all pass; BenchmarkFoldRequestHeavy parity with c9280b32 (11.31ms/47.5ms vs 11.31ms/48.4ms at 5k/20k). Companion statements follow for internal/statusview, ui/src/lib/api.ts and docs/concepts/staleness.md at the same head.","body":{"branch":"request/stale-because-row-v2","head":"eb64fbce6817576c55e0b0446fb41e8ab835cd44","path":"i